<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harris Treaty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1858</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Harris Treaty of 1858, formally the Treaty of Amity and Commerce, was concluded between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> through the American consul Townsend Harris. It opened ports to trade and granted extraterritoriality and fixed tariffs. Similar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unequal-treaties">unequal treaties</a> followed with other powers, provoking opposition that weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harris-treaty.jpg" alt="Harris Treaty" width="320" height="285" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: World Imaging · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Treaty_of_Amity_and_Commerce_between_Japan_and_the_United_States_29_July_1858.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
